	'k018951b1' => 'All employer communications are coordinated directly by Tomas Lindqvist, our employer liaison. Tomas manages appointment bookings, schedules Tuesday and Thursday workplace visits, clarifies invoicing, and ensures written plans arrive within 3 working days. Having a dedicated coordinator means management teams have a single reliable contact who understands their company\'s operational context and logistical requirements.',
	'k04106588' => 'Clinic &amp; access',
	'k06723103' => 'Clinic &amp; Access',
	'k06f71e82' => 'In this case, a manufacturing machinist experienced acute right shoulder pain caused by constant overhead reaching while operating an assembly press. Occupational Health Nurse &amp; Lead Assessor Samuel Osei evaluated his movement mechanics and referred him to our 6-week return-to-work programme under physiotherapist Ines Moreau. Ergonomist Kenji Arai visited the workshop and raised the machinist\'s bench height by 6 cm, which immediately eliminated awkward shoulder extension. Across 6 structured clinical sessions, the machinist rebuilt rotator cuff stability and completed modified duties. By week 7, he returned to full operational shifts without discomfort.',
	'k0749a134' => 'All health check appointments take approximately 45 minutes to complete. We ask employees to arrive five minutes before their scheduled time at our Westmere clinic. Please bring government-issued photo identification, any corrective eyewear or contact lenses used for work or driving, and an up-to-date list of current prescription medications. Wearing loose, comfortable clothing is recommended, as our clinicians will ask you to perform simple movements to evaluate active joint mobility.',
	'k07cf17bc' => 'Samuel conducts clinical strain assessments and workplace reviews, identifying physical hazards before they cause injury. His practical approach helps workers maintain mobility and comfort throughout their shifts.',
