	'k119e0c63' => 'These anonymised cases illustrate how Naru Clinic addresses physical strain across different workplace settings. In each case, clinical assessment and ergonomic adjustment restored comfortable working routines.',
	'k1386c752' => 'Naru Clinic provides five focused occupational health services designed for offices, workshops, and industrial plants. We combine direct clinical observation with practical workplace adaptations to keep teams healthy.',
	'k13f4c702' => 'In this case, our physiotherapist Ines Moreau designed a structured six-week rehabilitation programme combined with an ergonomic workstation review. Following six clinical sessions focused on rotator cuff strengthening and raising the lathe bench height by 6 centimetres, the machinist was able to resume full shifts in week seven.',
	'k16c11ab9' => 'For Employers',
	'k174b90ef' => '2F, 41 Foundry Lane, Westmere',
	'k178e3f41' => 'We provide transparent, fixed employer pricing across all occupational health services, enabling workplaces to plan preventative care and rehabilitation with complete clarity.',
	'k1f628e30' => 'Most chronic musculoskeletal injuries do not occur in an instant. They develop silently across months of repetitive reaching, awkward lifting, poor monitor positioning, or sustained static sitting. When an injured worker visits a standard medical clinic, treatment typically centers on rest and medication without examining the bench or chair that triggered the discomfort. Naru Clinic bridges this gap by connecting clinical evaluation directly to the working environment. We observe tools, lighting, bench heights, and daily routines. By understanding the mechanical demands placed on workers each shift, we help employers and employees introduce sensible workplace adjustments that protect health while keeping productivity intact.',
