	'k23e83b74' => 'In this case, a manufacturing machinist suffering from acute shoulder pain was referred to Naru Clinic after struggling with overhead assembly tasks. Ines Moreau enrolled him in the 6-week return-to-work programme. Working alongside ergonomist Kenji Arai, the team examined the machinist\'s workstation and raised the bench height by 6 cm. This mechanical change eliminated excessive shoulder extension. Supported by 6 rehabilitation sessions, the machinist successfully resumed full operational shifts in week 7 without symptoms.',
	'k244ecbae' => 'Our Clinical Team',
	'k248fb8bf' => '2F, 41 Foundry Lane, Westmere<br>+00 20 4410 7720<br>hello@naruclinic.example',
	'k249944f0' => 'When we opened Naru Clinic in 2012, our aim was straightforward: treat the physical cause of occupational strain rather than managing long-term absences after the fact. Over the years, our multidisciplinary team has confirmed that direct communication and timely ergonomic adjustments make all the difference. When an individual understands how their posture impacts their body and an employer is willing to adapt a workstation, recovery happens naturally. We remain committed to providing calm, precise, and practical occupational health care to every workplace we serve.',
	'k25d221bb' => 'We believe in straightforward, transparent pricing with no hidden charges. All services are charged in EUR excluding VAT: Individual strain assessment (60 min) at €140; Workplace walk-through for a half day covering up to 20 stations at €680; Return-to-work programme spanning 6 weeks and 6 sessions at €960; Pre-employment health check at €95; Periodic health check including hearing and vision at €120; and our Annual employer plan for up to 50 employees at €4,800 / year.',
