	'k3d4e6808' => 'How does the clinic protect employee medical confidentiality?',
	'k3f18e8bf' => 'Priya Natarajan',
	'k4151fc85' => 'Booking an Assessment or Walk-Through',
	'k42d908eb' => 'Kenji Arai is our clinic ergonomist, specializing in workplace walk-throughs and office desk ergonomics. He conducts Tuesday and Thursday site visits to evaluate equipment placement, bench elevations, seating mechanics, and tool handling across industrial and corporate settings. Kenji focuses on pragmatic, low-cost modifications—such as monitor arm repositioning or workstation height changes—that resolve postural stress without disrupting company workflows.',
	'k446f1095' => 'Periodic Health Monitoring',
	'k44e09931' => 'We help factories and offices identify physical strain early, before temporary discomfort turns into chronic injury or extended absence. Our occupational health team assesses workstations on site and provides clear, actionable recovery plans within three working days.',
	'k453aceb0' => 'Pages',
	'k4596b383' => 'Wrist',
	'k46d72bfb' => 'Direct Contact Information',
	'k478bfc55' => 'A pre-employment health check costs €95 and confirms that a candidate possesses the physical capabilities required for their prospective job role. The appointment takes 45 minutes at our clinic located at 2F, 41 Foundry Lane, Westmere. Lead assessor Samuel Osei reviews occupational medical history, measures vital signs, and examines joint mobility across the shoulder, lower back, and wrist. Employers receive prompt, objective certification of fitness for duty while respecting patient medical privacy.',
	'k495f3be8' => 'Programme Overview and Pricing',
	'k4963e802' => 'Prices in EUR, excl. VAT.',
	'k4ba07fdf' => 'Can small teams book individual assessments without an annual plan?',
	'k4c3880bb' => 'Method',
	'k4db67b9c' => 'A 20-minute clinical history exploring your specific tasks, physical symptoms, and previous joint or muscle strain.',
	'k4ee7e7a3' => 'Our clinical observations concentrate on the three anatomical areas most vulnerable to workplace strain: the shoulder, the lower back, and the wrist. Shoulder issues frequently stem from repetitive reaching or inappropriate bench heights. Lower back strain typically arises from static stooping, heavy pallet lifting, or unsupportive seating. Wrist discomfort commonly reflects repetitive keyboard entry, awkward mouse positioning, or vibrating manual tools. Pinpointing joint angles in these zones allows us to recommend precise workstation adjustments.',
	'k4f2fac7b' => 'Look',
	'k513615b1' => 'In this case, a warehouse picker suffered progressive lower back fatigue resulting from repetitive low pallet lifts and twisting motions during high-volume distribution shifts. Dr. Helena Varga conducted an initial examination and recommended placing the picker on modified duties for 4 weeks. Meanwhile, Kenji Arai worked directly with the warehouse logistics team on a Tuesday site visit to redesign the primary lifting station, installing elevated pallet stands. Supported by core conditioning sessions with Ines Moreau, the picker safely regained spinal endurance and resumed full picking duties without recurring fatigue.',
	'k519428e5' => 'Ines Moreau',
	'k51edaab1' => 'Accounts Team Wrist and Neck Postural Improvements',
	'k537752ea' => 'Workplace walk-through (half day, up to 20 stations)',
	'k5485cdba' => 'When contacting us, please state whether you require an individual strain assessment (€140), a half-day workplace walk-through for up to 20 stations (€680), a 6-week return-to-work programme (€960), or health screening services. Workplace visits take place on Tuesdays and Thursdays, while individual clinical consultations are scheduled throughout regular opening hours. We confirm appointment dates within one business day and provide completed written plans within 3 working days following assessment.',
	'k5b6c0d32' => 'Return-to-work programme (6 weeks, 6 sessions)',
	'k5d243cf6' => 'Occupational Health Nurse &amp; Lead Assessor',
	'k5dadb96b' => 'We are guided by three practical clinical principles across all our services. First, observation precedes intervention: we examine real postures and movement mechanics rather than relying on checklists or assumptions. Second, collaboration creates lasting change: we work alongside employees, line managers, and safety teams so that modifications are practical, accepted, and easy to maintain. Third, transparency builds trust: every worker receives honest feedback about their physical baseline, and every employer receives clear, actionable guidance without exaggerated claims or unnecessary procedures. This balanced methodology ensures that physical rehabilitation and workplace requirements support each other effectively.',
	'k5e6b67ae' => 'Warehouse Picker Lower Back Strain and Lifting Redesign',
	'k5e706a9b' => 'Visit',
	'k5fe82a73' => 'For employers — prices',
	'k62a76ba4' => 'Machinist Shoulder Strain and Bench Height Adjustment',
	'k66567e46' => 'Pre-employment health check',
	'k679bbd2a' => 'Read all cases',
	'k68063388' => 'Hearing and Vision Screening Procedures',
	'k68abc1bf' => 'Thorough individual evaluations and workstation walk-throughs to pinpoint repetitive strain risks and adjust physical demands before injuries develop.',
	'k68fbde08' => 'Technician Priya Natarajan oversees all audiometric and vision testing in our calibrated screening rooms. The hearing evaluation checks frequency responses across speech ranges to identify early signs of noise-induced hearing loss among industrial operators. Visual testing assesses near, distance, and peripheral clarity, which is essential for detailed assembly work and sustained computer usage. Priya ensures that testing is calm, rapid, and accurate, explaining results clearly to every employee.',
	'k69aa5f60' => 'Health Checks &amp; Screenings',
	'k6a40144b' => 'Led by ergonomist Kenji Arai, our office and desk ergonomics service addresses postural discomfort caused by screen-based work. We evaluate monitor heights, seating support, keyboard angles, and desk spacing across individual desks or entire administrative teams. By recommending practical modifications such as adjustable monitor arms, footrests, and structured micro-break schedules, we relieve persistent neck and wrist tension. These straightforward adjustments enhance daily comfort and help administrative personnel maintain healthy posture throughout their working day.',
	'k6a7e7316' => 'Hours',
	'k6b998305' => 'Detailed workstation reviews, screen alignments, and movement routines that alleviate persistent neck, shoulder, and wrist tension.',
	'k6bdfed09' => 'The return-to-work programme at Naru Clinic costs €960 and consists of 6 individual sessions scheduled across 6 consecutive weeks. Managed by registered physiotherapist Ines Moreau, the service is designed for employees recovering from musculoskeletal injuries, including shoulder pain, lower back episodes, and repetitive strain. Instead of keeping recovering workers completely away from work until symptoms disappear, we create a safe, gradual pathway that coordinates physical recovery with workplace duty modifications.',
	'k6dbef858' => 'Ines Moreau is a registered physiotherapist who directs our 6-week return-to-work programmes. She designs tailored exercise regimes that rebuild muscular strength and joint stability while coordinating gradual increases in workplace responsibilities with employers. Ines believes that phased recovery within the actual working environment builds long-term physical confidence and prevents recurring strain. Her supportive, structured sessions ensure workers resume full duties safely.',
	'k6e2a63dd' => 'Whether you are an employer looking to review a workstation setup or an employee managing persistent physical discomfort, contact our clinic team today. We assess individual cases and schedule workplace walk-throughs promptly.',
	'k6f218bbf' => 'Contact Naru Clinic to arrange individual assessments, book on-site workplace walk-throughs, or discuss employer healthcare plans. Our reception and coordination team is here to assist.',
