	'k713fad3b' => 'Our Story Since 2012',
	'k73c9be44' => 'Naru Clinic is a fictional practice. Prices in EUR, excluding VAT.',
	'k75aeaa25' => 'Five ways we keep people at work',
	'k77567cdd' => 'A factory machinist experienced persistent shoulder pain whenever lifting heavy metal components onto his lathe. As the discomfort intensified over several months, he began modifying his grip, which introduced secondary neck stiffness and slowed his daily output. Rather than waiting until the joint seized completely, his supervisor arranged an occupational strain assessment with our clinic.',
	'k78413552' => 'What we do',
	'k7c762c38' => 'We offer pre-employment health checks for €95 and periodic health checks for €120, which include comprehensive hearing and vision screening. Each appointment requires approximately 45 minutes at our Westmere clinic. These assessments establish clear baseline health records, confirm an individual\'s physical fitness for specific operating roles, and monitor long-term occupational wellbeing. Employers receive objective clinical fitness certificates, while employees gain valuable personal awareness of their cardiovascular and musculoskeletal health.',
	'k80b2d776' => 'Dr. Helena Varga',
	'k81d148bc' => 'Who coordinates employee appointments and company reporting?',
	'k8370f7d6' => 'Workplace walk-throughs take place on Tuesdays and Thursdays. Lead assessor Samuel Osei and ergonomist Kenji Arai spend a half day at your facility observing up to 20 work stations in active operation. They observe posture, reach heights, lifting mechanics, and repetitive actions on factory lines or office floors, discussing physical comfort with workers to identify where equipment adjustments can reduce daily strain.',
	'k838f716d' => 'Naru Clinic was established in 2012 by Dr. Helena Varga, an experienced occupational physician and our medical director. After years of observing how standard clinical settings fail to account for the physical realities of daily employment, Dr. Varga created a dedicated clinic tailored specifically to workplaces. Based at 41 Foundry Lane in Westmere, our practice began by serving nearby industrial facilities and office teams. Over the past decade, we have built a collaborative clinical environment where physicians, nurses, physiotherapists, and ergonomists work together. Our focus has remained unchanged: identifying physical strain at the workstation before it requires formal sick leave.',
	'k83cb4c14' => 'Shoulder',
	'k862c79ab' => 'Naru Clinic delivers thorough pre-employment and periodic health assessments for local businesses. We provide accurate baseline evaluations and certified screening to support workplace safety.',
	'k8805b5f9' => 'Return to work',
	'k88fa4852' => 'Step-Free Access and Facilities',
