	'k8b43f2d8' => 'Health checks',
	'k8da2756d' => 'Workplace Walk-Throughs and Individual Reviews',
	'k8de17dee' => 'Closed Sundays and public holidays',
	'k8eea85a8' => 'Our periodic health check costs €120 and includes integrated hearing and vision screening alongside a physical examination. Designed for established staff, periodic checks detect subtle changes in musculoskeletal flexibility, hearing thresholds, and visual acuity caused by operational conditions. By benchmarking results annually, employers can identify workplace risks early, verify that personal protective equipment remains effective, and protect experienced workers from developing chronic work-related ailments over their careers.',
	'k8f78cfba' => 'In most workplaces, physical injury rarely happens all at once. It begins quietly with an awkward lift at a packing bench, a screen set two inches too low, or a shoulder that aches slightly by Thursday afternoon. Because workers often push through discomfort to meet production targets, repetitive physical strain builds over months without formal medical attention.',
	'k8f7f4c1c' => 'About',
	'k8fe613ad' => 'Our workplace strain assessments pinpoint biomechanical stress before it leads to injury. Available as an individual 60-minute assessment for €140 or a comprehensive half-day workplace walk-through covering up to 20 stations for €680, this service evaluates real working postures. Clinicians analyze shoulder reach, lower back alignment, and wrist flexion during active tasks. Following the visit, we deliver a written report outlining specific station adjustments to both the worker and, with their consent, the employer within 3 working days.',
	'k916b362a' => 'Naru Clinic is situated at 2F, 41 Foundry Lane, Westmere. Our clinic is open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 and Saturday from 08:30 to 12:30. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. On-site workplace walk-throughs and corporate visits are conducted on Tuesdays and Thursdays. For appointment enquiries, corporate bookings, or access questions, please call our reception team at +00 20 4410 7720 or send an email to hello@naruclinic.example.',
	'k9225e64e' => 'Dr. Helena Varga is our medical director, occupational physician, and the founder of Naru Clinic in 2012. She directs clinical governance, oversees pre-employment standards, and leads medical reviews for complex cases. Dr. Varga believes that effective occupational medicine requires understanding the exact mechanical demands placed on workers during their daily shifts. She collaborates closely with local employers and clinic staff to ensure all assessments provide practical, medically sound outcomes.',
	'k9398ea04' => 'Reaching our clinic is straightforward whether travelling by public transit or private vehicle. Westmere railway station is located an eight-minute walk away, providing regular regional train services. Bus routes stop directly at the Foundry Lane junction every fifteen minutes during clinic hours. For those arriving by car, designated visitor parking bays are available adjacent to 41 Foundry Lane, including dedicated drop-off spaces situated right beside the front building entrance.',
	'k992a0f05' => 'Services',
	'k99338888' => 'Within 3 working days of the assessment, both the worker and, with their consent, the employer receive a concise, written modification plan. The report details observed mechanical risk factors and outlines clear, feasible remedies. Recommendations prioritize low-cost physical changes, such as adjusting bench elevations, repositioning storage racks, or introducing monitor arms, alongside practical pacing routines. This ensures employers can implement effective health improvements without disrupting production or purchasing unnecessary equipment.',
	'k99664fda' => 'Founded in 2012, Naru Clinic provides dedicated occupational health care for factory and office workplaces. We believe that clinical observation of physical working conditions prevents injury and preserves long-term wellbeing.',
	'k9a5ec51a' => 'Pre-Employment and Periodic Health Checks',
	'k9b2a87a2' => 'Samuel Osei',
	'k9cc84831' => 'Periodic health check (incl. hearing &amp; vision)',
	'k9cfc9b74' => 'Contact Us',
	'k9d08ac5e' => 'Clinic',
	'k9f13f6e9' => 'Annual employer plan (up to 50 employees)',
	'k9f9be0c5' => 'Following any individual strain assessment or on-site workplace walk-through, our clinical team delivers a concise written plan within 3 working days. The report is provided directly to the employee and, once they have provided written consent, to their employer. It outlines practical physical adjustments to equipment, bench heights, and task schedules that can be implemented immediately without causing operational delays.',
	'ka02e6898' => 'The clinic &amp; people',
	'ka0dfca75' => 'Naru Clinic is located in Westmere, providing modern clinical facilities for individual assessments and employee health screenings. We offer step-free access and convenient local transport connections.',
	'ka231fd85' => 'Our workplace assessments evaluate physical demands directly where staff perform their daily duties. We observe real movement mechanics to recommend practical adjustments that prevent strain.',
	'ka3129344' => 'Transport Links and Parking',
	'ka4b7c0d9' => 'A practical, written plan delivered to the worker and, with consent, the employer within 3 working days.',
	'ka4f5a999' => 'Why We Focus on the Workplace',
	'ka5ec0f75' => 'Strain shows up long before the sick note.',
	'ka68af669' => 'You can reach Naru Clinic by calling +00 20 4410 7720 or by emailing hello@naruclinic.example. Our clinic is located at 2F, 41 Foundry Lane, Westmere. Reception desk hours are Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 and Saturday from 08:30 to 12:30. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. Employer liaison Tomas Lindqvist is available during weekday hours to assist corporate clients with booking assessments and organizing annual healthcare plans.',
	'ka6f9dd25' => 'Employers',
	'ka9098cdc' => 'Talk, look, visit, plan.',
	'ka97e362c' => 'About Naru Clinic',
	'ka9a95a48' => 'Case stories',
	'kac1fca1b' => 'By the time an employee takes sick leave, recovery is longer, harder, and more disruptive for everyone involved. Addressing muscle tension, joint strain, and workstation mechanics at the first sign of discomfort keeps workers healthy and avoids weeks of lost production.',
	'kac8158a3' => '41 Foundry Lane, Westmere',
	'kac848fa2' => 'Team',
	'kade05991' => 'Medical Director &amp; Occupational Physician',
	'kafda9fc6' => 'The 6-week progression is structured into three distinct clinical phases. In Weeks 1 and 2, Ines Moreau assesses baseline capacity, initiates gentle mobility exercises, and recommends temporary light duties. In Weeks 3 and 4, sessions focus on physical conditioning and real workplace testing, verifying that adjusted station heights or altered tool handling reduce physical strain. During Weeks 5 and 6, the worker builds stamina on full shifts while receiving final movement coaching to ensure lasting workplace comfort.',
	'kb31976c2' => 'Conducted by technician Priya Natarajan, our sensory screening identifies early changes in visual acuity and auditory thresholds. Screenings are conducted in dedicated, sound-controlled testing rooms using calibrated diagnostic equipment. This service is vital for personnel exposed to noisy machinery on factory floors or sustained screen glare in office facilities. Regular monitoring enables safety coordinators to verify the effectiveness of hearing protection and ensure adequate lighting across every operational department.',
	'kb3295f53' => 'Mon–Fri 08:00–18:00<br>Sat 08:30–12:30<br>Closed Sundays and public holidays',
	'kb7b07f8e' => 'We follow a straightforward four-step process to understand how daily work impacts your body and to put practical solutions in place without delay.',
