	'kd7663fa4' => 'Talk',
	'kd7fca18d' => 'Hearing and Vision Screening',
	'kd98a1266' => 'For employers',
	'kdb09ad69' => 'Founder of Naru Clinic, Dr. Varga guides clinical governance and advises leadership on workplace health management. She has directed occupational medicine initiatives across industrial and office facilities since 2012.',
	'kdc6450cb' => 'How quickly do we receive the assessment plan?',
	'kdcfc0cdd' => 'Hearing &amp; vision screening',
	'kdd7bf230' => 'Address',
	'kde7af71f' => 'The clinical team at Naru Clinic combines medical expertise, ergonomics, physiotherapy, and healthcare administration. We work together to assess and resolve physical workplace strain.',
	'kde949fed' => '€4,800 / year',
	'kdf0f20d6' => 'Problem',
	'ke026f2f9' => 'Structured six-week recovery schedules coordinating clinical rehabilitation with modified duties to help recovering staff resume full duties safely.',
	'ke1421e45' => 'Case Summary: Machinist Shoulder Rehabilitation',
	'ke1e227b1' => 'Naru Clinic adheres to strict medical confidentiality standards. Clinical records, detailed diagnoses, and personal medical histories remain entirely confidential between the worker and our clinical staff. Reports shared with employers focus exclusively on practical workplace modifications, fitness for duty, and ergonomic recommendations. We only share modification plans with company management after obtaining the worker\'s explicit written consent.',
	'ke3a4dda7' => 'Tomas Lindqvist',
	'ke3f6e6c0' => 'Tomas Lindqvist serves as our employer liaison and coordinator, managing administrative partnerships between Naru Clinic and business clients. He organizes on-site walk-through schedules, coordinates staff appointments, and ensures assessment reports reach designated managers within 3 working days. Tomas provides a dependable, responsive contact point for human resources and safety managers seeking clear guidance on occupational health services.',
	'ke498f850' => 'Workplace Strain Assessment',
	'ke4a9dcc2' => 'Plan in your hands within 3 working days.',
	'ke64392e8' => '6 sessions',
	'ke71bbaa4' => 'Annual Employer Healthcare Plan',
	'ke8edfd9a' => 'Samuel Osei is our occupational health nurse and lead assessor, carrying out primary strain assessments at our Westmere clinic and on factory floors. He evaluates movement ranges and posture across the shoulder, lower back, and wrist to identify strain before injury occurs. Samuel works closely with individual workers to understand their symptoms and translates clinical observations into clear, practical recommendations within 3 working days.',
	'ke9eed86d' => 'Naru Clinic partners with businesses across Westmere to deliver clear occupational health services and fixed-price medical assessments. We help managers reduce sick leave and maintain ergonomic, productive workplaces.',
	'kf31eecad' => 'Appointment Preparation and What to Bring',
	'kf333da9f' => 'Pre-Employment Health Checks',
	'kf62a213f' => 'Yes. Businesses of any size can access our occupational health services on an ad-hoc basis without enrolling in an annual contract. You can book a single individual strain assessment for €140 or schedule a half-day walk-through for €680 whenever an employee reports discomfort or after introducing new equipment. This flexibility ensures small enterprises receive expert clinical support exactly when required.',
	'kf8cb2108' => 'Naru Clinic offers two assessment formats to accommodate different workplace scales. Employers can book an individual strain assessment lasting 60 minutes for €140, ideal for resolving a specific worker\'s persistent discomfort. Alternatively, organizations can schedule a half-day workplace walk-through covering up to 20 stations for €680. Conducted on Tuesdays and Thursdays, walk-throughs allow ergonomist Kenji Arai and nurse Samuel Osei to observe operational rhythms, tooling layouts, and physical postures directly on the shop floor or office suite.',
	'kf9296ea1' => 'Physiotherapist Ines Moreau acts as the clinical anchor for every participant. She works in close communication with medical director Dr. Helena Varga and occupational health nurse Samuel Osei to evaluate physical milestones. Simultaneously, employer liaison Tomas Lindqvist keeps company managers informed about recommended shift adaptations. This collaborative approach ensures that supervisor expectations match the employee\'s current clinical recovery stage, eliminating misunderstandings and building mutual confidence throughout the rehabilitation process.',
	'kf9413da7' => 'Baseline health assessments and regular employee medical reviews tailored to specific occupational risks and statutory requirements.',
	'kfa4830af' => 'In this case, an accounting team of fourteen people reported persistent wrist discomfort, neck tightness, and afternoon headaches during extended financial audit cycles. Kenji Arai conducted a half-day office assessment, evaluating 14 desks in one morning. He identified static neck flexion and wrist extension linked to rigid display screens and improper chair heights. Two adjustable monitor arms were fitted, desk chairs were realigned, and Priya Natarajan checked screen visual distances. With the addition of a structured hourly micro-break routine, the team reported notable relief from neck and wrist tension.',
